srem-s: x % y, signed, for x from -999 to 999 and y from -999 to 999 but not 0.
Cells 75-98. To call it, put y in cell 92, load x into the accumulator and JMP 75.
It returns x % y in the accumulator.
It overwrites its own cells and cell 99, including y in cell 92 (made |y|).
Size 24 cells. It runs at most 3,013 instructions, 22.7 on average, counted from cell 75 to the return jump in cell 98.
Exact over the domain.

cell  contents   notes
 75     691      STO 91   cells 75-77: the call: store x, and copy the return jump from cell 99 into cell 98
 76     199      CLA 99
 77     698      STO 98
 78     192      CLA 92   cells 78-79: y < 0: make it -y
 79     387      TAC 87
 80     191      CLA 91   cells 80-86: x >= 0: take y away until below 0, then add it back
 81     393      TAC 93
 82     792      SUB 92
 83     385      TAC 85
 84     882      JMP 82
 85     292      ADD 92
 86     898      JMP 98
 87     792      SUB 92   cells 87-90: y = -y
 88     792      SUB 92
 89     692      STO 92
 90     880      JMP 80
 91     000      data: x
 92     000      data: y, made |y|
 93     700      SUB 00   cells 93-97: x < 0: from r - 1, add y while r + y <= 0, then back to r
 94     292      ADD 92
 95     394      TAC 94
 96     792      SUB 92
 97     200      ADD 00
 98     000               set on every call: the jump back to the caller
